From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov5648: expose the orientation and rotation properties

Parse the standard orientation and rotation firmware properties and expose
them as the V4L2_CID_CAMERA_ORIENTATION and V4L2_CID_CAMERA_SENSOR_ROTATION
controls, as most sensor drivers do, so that userspace (libcamera) can tell
which side of the device the sensor faces and how it is mounted.

Let the binding accept the properties by referencing video-interface-devices.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN or_a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/ovti,ov5648.yaml or_b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/ovti,ov5648.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/ovti,ov5648.yaml	2026-09-18 21:00:41.126972804 +0200
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/ovti,ov5648.yaml	2026-09-18 21:00:41.147775315 +0200
@@ -9,6 +9,9 @@
 maintainers:
   - Paul Kocialkowski <paul.kocialkowski@bootlin.com>
 
+allOf:
+  - $ref: /schemas/media/video-interface-devices.yaml#
+
 properties:
   compatible:
     const: ovti,ov5648
@@ -66,7 +69,7 @@
   - dovdd-supply
   - port
 
-additionalProperties: false
+unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 examples:
   - |
diff -ruN or_a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5648.c or_b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5648.c
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5648.c	2026-09-18 21:00:41.125163588 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5648.c	2026-09-18 21:00:41.147615443 +0200
@@ -2126,6 +2126,7 @@
 	struct ov5648_ctrls *ctrls = &sensor->ctrls;
 	struct v4l2_ctrl_handler *handler = &ctrls->handler;
 	const struct v4l2_ctrl_ops *ops = &ov5648_ctrl_ops;
+	struct v4l2_fwnode_device_properties props;
 	int ret;
 
 	v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(handler, 32);
@@ -2224,6 +2225,16 @@
 		v4l2_ctrl_new_std(handler, NULL, V4L2_CID_PIXEL_RATE, 1,
 				  INT_MAX, 1, 1);
 
+	/* Orientation and rotation from the firmware node */
+
+	ret = v4l2_fwnode_device_parse(sensor->dev, &props);
+	if (ret)
+		goto error_ctrls;
+
+	ret = v4l2_ctrl_new_fwnode_properties(handler, ops, &props);
+	if (ret)
+		goto error_ctrls;
+
 	if (handler->error) {
 		ret = handler->error;
 		goto error_ctrls;
